{#- One stance's description (`store/turn_plan.py`, roadmap 02 §6.1): the
    option text the turn decision is offered beside the id, and the clause
    the intent block (`scene/turn_intent.j2`) tells the writer. Var: stance
    (one of `turn_plan.STANCES`). A stance is a way of answering, never what
    the character says. -#}
{%- if stance == "engage" -%}
answer or go along openly
{%- elif stance == "press" -%}
push, challenge or accuse
{%- elif stance == "deflect" -%}
evade, change the subject, or answer a different question
{%- elif stance == "refuse" -%}
decline openly
{%- elif stance == "deceive" -%}
say something they believe is untrue
{%- elif stance == "withdraw" -%}
disengage, go quiet, or leave the exchange
{%- elif stance == "act" -%}
let an action carry the reply rather than words
{%- endif -%}
